<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>06 · METHOD — ARMS</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Four arms, one variable each — 962 records behind them
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 46, marginTop: 24 }}>
        <Box style={{ width: 470, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#7E93AE', letterSpacing: 1.4, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>EVERY NUMBER TRAVELS THE SAME PATH</Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', marginTop: 12 }}>
                {[
                    ['Raw data', '3 public benchmarks, licence and md5 recorded'],
                    ['Frozen splits', 'official indices where published, hashed and versioned'],
                    ['One arm at a time', 'A1 / A2 / A3 / A4 ride the same rows and seeds'],
                    ['One record per run', 'R², MAE, RMSE, wall clock, predictions, hashes'],
                    ['Λ per cell, κ per dataset', 'aggregated only after a four-way reconciliation gate'],
                ].map(([head, sub], i) => (
                    <Box key={head} style={{ flexDirection: 'column' }}>
                        {i > 0 ? <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#33445F', lineHeight: 1.3, marginTop: 5, marginBottom: 5 }}>↓</Text> : null}
                        <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'column', padding: '9px 14px', background: i === 2 ? '#16233A' : '#111B2E', border: '1px solid ' + (i === 2 ? '#2F4A75' : '#24334C'), borderRadius: 5 }}>
                            <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#FFFFFF', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>{head}</Text>
                            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#8FA3BC', marginTop: 2 }}>{sub}</Text>
                        </Box>
                    </Box>
                ))}
            </Box>
        </Box>

        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column' }}>
            <Table
                style={{ width: 644, height: 300 }}
                defaultTextStyle={{ fontSize: 13, textAlign: 'left', color: '#C3D0E2' }}
                defaultCellStyle={{ border: { bottom: { width: 1, color: '#1D2A40' } }, background: { color: '#0E1728' } }}
                cells={[
                    [
                        { text: 'Arm', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 12 }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                        { text: 'What it changes', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 12 }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                        { text: 'Runs', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 12, textAlign: 'right' }, cellStyle: { background: { color: '#16233A' } } },
                    ],
                    [
                        { text: 'A1 floor', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#8FA3BC' } },
                        'Predicts the training mean — reference only',
                        { text: '48', textStyle: { color: '#8FA3BC', textAlign: 'right' } },
                    ],
                    [
                        { text: 'A2 unit', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FFFFFF' } },
                        '205 RDKit descriptors + 2048-bit fingerprint → XGBoost, 30 tuning trials',
                        { text: '328', textStyle: { color: '#FFFFFF', textAlign: 'right' } },
                    ],
                    [
                        { text: 'A3 chain', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#4D8DFF' } },
                        'chemprop 2.1.0 MPNN — official hyper-parameters, tuned zero times',
                        { text: '538', textStyle: { color: '#4D8DFF', textAlign: 'right' } },
                    ],
                    [
                        { text: 'A4 chain', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#4D8DFF' } },
                        'polyBERT frozen encoder + ridge head (capacity capped)',
                        { text: '48', textStyle: { color: '#4D8DFF', textAlign: 'right' } },
                    ],
                    [
                        { text: 'A5 chain', textStyle: { bold: true, color: '#FF6B6B' } },
                        'Would inject chain input at a fixed architecture',
                        { text: '0', textStyle: { color: '#FF6B6B', textAlign: 'right', bold: true } },
                    ],
                ]}
            />
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#7E93AE', marginTop: 10, lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
                A5 is zero because its inputs do not exist in the data — see slide 13. It is logged as not constructible, never as "no gain".
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>
            Gate before any table is written: 4,896 provenance checks — 4,832 ok / 64 exempt / 0 fail.
        </Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#5E7590' }}>7 / 17</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
